IBM Bob was used as an AI-assisted development tool in the Student_Tutor project to support the design, development, and improvement of the application. It helped in reducing development time and making the overall workflow more efficient.  IBM Bob was used to assist with different development activities such as generating and improving code, creating application components, identifying errors, and suggesting solutions during development. It helped in developing the basic structure of the Student_Tutor platform and implementing important functionalities required for both students and tutors.  The development workflow started with defining the requirements of the Student_Tutor system, including student registration, tutor registration, profile management, subject selection, tutor searching, class scheduling, and communication between students and tutors. IBM Bob was then used to assist in converting these requirements into appropriate technical components and code.  One of the key uses of IBM Bob was AI-assisted code generation. It helped generate code for different modules and provided suggestions for implementing required features. This reduced repetitive coding work and allowed development to focus more on the functionality and user experience of the platform.  IBM Bob was also used for debugging and error identification. During development, errors or unexpected behaviour could be analyzed with the help of AI-generated suggestions. This helped in identifying possible causes of errors and improving the code accordingly.  Another important use was code improvement and optimization. IBM Bob helped review code and suggest cleaner, more maintainable approaches. This was useful for creating a structured project in which different modules could be developed and managed independently.  For the Student_Tutor workflow, IBM Bob assisted in developing features such as:  Student and tutor registration and login Student and tutor profile management Subject and course-related functionality Tutor search and selection Class or session scheduling Database-related operations Form validation Backend logic and API development Error handling and debugging Improving code structure and maintainability
